3. How to View the Data on Google Analytics (Step-by-Step for You & Your Boss)
Google Analytics 4 (GA4) is 100% free and provides the official live dashboard:

Step 1: Get your free Measurement ID
Go to analytics.google.com and log in with any Google account.
Click Start measuring and type your website name (SARVIKA).
Under Data Streams, choose Web and enter your website URL.
Google will give you a Measurement ID that looks like: G-XXXXXXXXXX.
Step 2: Paste the ID into the project
Open 

src/utils/analytics.js
 and paste your ID:

javascript
export const GA_MEASUREMENT_ID = 'G-XXXXXXXXXX'; // Replace with your real ID
Step 3: Where you and your boss will see the data
Inside Google Analytics:

World Map of Visitors: Click Reports → Demographics → Demographic details. You will see a world map highlighting UK, India, and other countries with visitor numbers.
Realtime Live Traffic: Click Reports → Realtime to see live users currently on the site and which city/country they are browsing from.
Demo Form Submissions: Click Reports → Engagement → Events to see the generate_lead events broken down by country.